red his power after  years and years of training  so to take it from him and give it to  the untrained derby would probably be  the stupidest thing they could do  in theory i guess if they free dr garaki  he could make a duplicate version of  getting squirk and then give that copy  to toya  but there is a much easier way for him  to get an upgrade within the todoroki  family there are three potential  candidates who could have their ice  quilts transferred to derby  and those are rey fiumi and natsuo  starting with rey it's all but confirmed  that her ability is the exact same with  shoto's ice creation  as we saw her use it to cool his face  down after she threw the boiling water  during the sports festival shoto will  also explicitly refer to his icy side as  her quirk  which is something you wouldn't really  say unless it's the same on top of that  when endeavour was younger he was  looking for someone to have a quirk  marriage with  and it stands to reason that he only  approached rey in the first place  because she has such a great power  moving on to fuyumi now chapter 291  stated that she inherited that same  quirk but naturally endeavour didn't  train her since he wanted a child who  had ice and fire  natsuwa was born years later and while  it's not outright said what his quirk is  everything implies that he generates ice  like everyone else this means debbie has  several options when choosing which  todoroki to steal a quirk from  and whoever he picks would likely be the  one that would hurt endeavour the most  the paranormal liberation war proves  that toyo feels nothing for anyone in  the todoroki family  as he even regretted that nacho wasn't  killed by one of the villains he sent to  their location  so all that matters to him is hurting  endeavor and he'll do whatever he can to  make that happen  whether it's killing shoto revealing the  truth about their past or stealing the  quirk of someone he loves  the villains easily have enough  resources to kidnap one member of the  todorokis and harvest their quirk  and i think endeavour would be most hurt  if they kidnapped for yumi  i say this because she was always the  one trying to hold the family together  when everything was a mess  and she was also usually the one sibling  who tried to get along with their dad  if the yumi is held hostage by the  liberation front then she'd likely try  to get through to her brother and make  him see what he's doing is wrong  however given that he's a crazy person i  doubt it'd make much of a difference  shigoraki could then upgrade darby by  doing a quirk transfer using all for one  and part of me thinks she would allow it  to be taken without putting up any  resistance  she'd know she has no chance fighting  back against the villains and on some  level i think fuumi understands why toya  is trying to hurt endeavour  even if she doesn't agree with his  methods after the transfer is done  they'd likely keep her as a hostage to  use as leverage against the number one  hero  because if they threaten to kill her or  turn her into a nomu then it might make  him never hesitate  anyway with fiumi's eyes toy would  become a mirror image of shoto  as they both possess the exact same  capabilities whereas one sibling is the  natural-born creation the endeavor  wanted  darby could be the evil frankenstein  version that's the result of his  terrible parenting  from a young age toy was told he had the  potential to surpass all might  only to then be told he couldn't be a  hero once he started getting burns  and in his mind his father replaced him  with shoto  this is funny because rey warned  endeavor that having more kids to make  them heroes would be too painful for  toya  but he went and did it anyway and i see  what derby could be the final  consequence of that decision  when they come face to face he could  taunt his father over the fact he stole  for yumi's quirk  and that would definitely make endeavour  suffer more than anything toy ha